*****

Set generic terminal mode options and meanings of special characters to their
default settings:

$ stty sane

Initialize a terminal's settings using its terminfo entry:

$ tput init

Reset a terminal's settings using its terminfo entry:

$ tput reset

*****

The standalone "reset" command is a symlink to tset.  tset is provided by
termcap, which predates terminfo.

*****

One effect of running "reset" is that the clocal flag for the terminal is
turned off (i.e. stty -a will show "-clocal").  This can cause some terminal
getty processes to hang when a user session logout occurs.  To avoid this
problem, either use terminal setting commands other than "reset" or run "stty
clocal" on the terminal before logging out a user session.  If the getty
process becomes hung, run "stty -F /dev/tty... clocal" on the getty server
host, substituting the affected terminal name for /dev/tty....

*****

In some cases, nothing short of bouncing the terminal listener process (getty)
or power-cycling a physical terminal will suffice to correct a malfunctioning
terminal connection.
